# TF-903: Fix the formatting and vet complaints in report.go

## Goal

The file report.go in this Go module is not formatted the way gofmt formats Go
source and it also contains a call that go vet complains about, so the goal of
this task is to repair both problems, so that gofmt lists no files and go vet
reports no complaints, while the behaviour of the program stays exactly the
same as it is now.

## Dependencies

None

## Scope

Edit only report.go. Format it with gofmt, and change the Printf call that
passes a wrong number of arguments for its format string so that the format and
its arguments match. Do not change what the program prints, apart from the
fixed formatting verb.

## Constraints

Do not edit any test, do not add dependencies, do not touch any file other than
report.go, and make sure the change is committed to the task branch once the
checks have passed.

## Success criteria

### C1: gofmt lists no files

Check: test -z "$(gofmt -l .)"

### C2: go vet is clean

Check: go vet ./...

### C3: The unit tests pass

Check: go test ./...

## Verification

Run each check from the repository root and report its exit code, and also run
the project wrappers when they exist, reporting the exit code of each.
